Package: bootei
Type: Package
Title: Bootstrap Ensemble Tie-Breaking for Permutation Tests
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Giovanni",
        family = "Corradini",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        email = "corradini@leibniz-bips.de"
    )
Description: Implements Bootstrap Ensemble Inference (BOOTEI), a generic refinement
    for discrete permutation tests in low-resolution settings such as small sample
    sizes, sparse contingency tables, few outcome levels, and pervasive ties.
    The method preserves the original permutation test statistic and augments it
    with a bootstrap ensemble score used solely for deterministic tie-breaking
    in the permutation reference distribution. By reusing a fixed bootstrap plan
    across permutations, BOOTEI retains finite-sample validity under exchangeability
    and produces permutation p-values that are never larger than those obtained
    from the classical permutation test.
